// AurOS: automatic security updates for everything, the kernel, grub
// and shim included.
//
// Until 2026-10 these three were blacklisted here, because Ubuntu's
// update-grub would have replaced AurOS's start-up menu (and with it
// "Put Windows back") and grub-install would have reordered BootOrder.
// Both are diverted to /usr/lib/auros/bootchain now (build/forge,
// stage 3): kernel updates rewrite AurOS's own menu with the previous
// kernel as an automatic fallback, and a new shim or grub is installed
// on AurOS's EFI partition only after checking this firmware trusts it
// (the Microsoft 2011 -> 2023 key change) and its SBAT level allows it.
// tools/bootchaintest.sh is the proof.
//
// Leaving them out was not the safe side: a grub that SBAT revokes
// later, by a Windows update writing the firmware's revocation level,
// is a computer that stops starting AurOS one morning.
// (No Package-Blacklist: nothing is held back.)
